# lanyard default development signing key — PUBLIC AND FORGEABLE ON PURPOSE.
#
# This key is committed to the lanyard repository so that a fresh install with
# no data dir produces the same kid and the same public key every time
# (CONCEPT §8). Anyone holding the binary can therefore mint a token that
# lanyard's JWKS will validate.
#
# That is correct for a development IdP and it is why the default bind is
# loopback. Never expose lanyard to a network you do not trust. To use your own
# key, replace <data-dir>/signing-key.pem with any PKCS#8 RSA private key; the
# kid follows it automatically.
